d5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 378966, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01CYSwunLND3ZAWDdDeoXWo6", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 378966, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01CYSwunLND3ZAWDdDeoXWo6", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383116, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding, which rounds a half-cent to the nearest even cent. It now gives 2.665 \u2192 2.66 and 2.675 \u2192 2.68, which is what the test expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212, but the advisory system didn't recognise it, so I relied on the docstring and the test.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by looking at the relevant files.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019rXsBjuRcqoyYd3ew67YLB", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01LqAR4M5fiCrfCTecLcQbTr", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_016bFte3S4rHt7aDgbJKvpzL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212", "confidence": 0.8}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The fix is clear: the docstring says ROUND_HALF_EVEN but the code uses ROUND_HALF_UP. (2.675 \u2192 2.68 and 2.665 \u2192 2.66 are both consistent with half-even.) Creating a branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01PX4ZVDHADYDZcgygK6x2s1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_017wTSFwj684Sp76PuwUpQpx", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}], "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01V64Po9K6jknFgpsn1ZYBrg", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_015SYJndxCgEcJUxAmighay1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Opening the PR.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01CYSwunLND3ZAWDdDeoXWo6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212", "body": "The nightly build was failing because `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` expects banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP` despite its docstring saying otherwise.\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, so e.g. `2.665 -> 2.66` and `2.675 -> 2.68`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug on a new branch, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` rounded half-cents up (`ROUND_HALF_UP`), even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`) per FIN-212. That's why `tests/test_money.py` failed: 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **The fix:** On branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed it to banker's rounding, which rounds a half-cent to the nearest even cent. It now gives 2.665 \u2192 2.66 and 2.675 \u2192 2.68, which is what the test expects.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI tried to look up FIN-212, but the advisory system didn't recognise it, so I relied on the docstring and the test.\n\nI haven't merged the PR. Merging into main needs a code owner's approval.", "type": "text"}